    "text": "beUI Native is free — Pro mobile blocks and screens are in presale from $99\n\nReserve\nbeUI Pro for mobile\nbeUI\nComponents\nBlocks\nAgents\nCharts\nPlayground\nSponsors\nLight theme\nLight theme\nDark theme\nDark theme\nSystem theme\nSystem theme\n1.9k\nGet Pro\nAll\nAgents\nComponents\nBlocks\n\nINTRO\n\nHome\nChangelog\n\nGUIDES\n\nMotion Guides\nAgent Guide\nOpenUI\nReact Native Setup\nAI AGENTS\n18\nVoice Orb\nMessage Bubble\nMessage\nMessage Scroller\nPrompt Input\nTodo List\nCode Block\nApproval Card\nFile Diff\nTool Result\nStreaming Response\nImage Generation\nTool Approval\nCitations\nAgent Activity\nAgent Loading States\nAI Sidebar\nChat App\nCOMPONENTS\n54\nTimeline\nNEW\nAnimated Alert\nAnimated Collapsible\nAspect Ratio\nArc Picker\nSortable List\nImage Viewer\nDate Range Picker\nCard\nColor Picker\nAnimated Color Selector\nAnimated Breadcrumb\nTilt Card\nButton\nAnimated CTA Buttons\nExpandable Control\nAdaptive Stepper\nMarquee\nTabs\nSwitch\nInput\nSelect\nCombobox\nMulti Select\nCheckbox\nRadio Group\nBottom Sheet\nPull to Refresh\nShared Layout Background\nBounce Sidebar\nAnimated Sidebar\nFile Tree\nPreview Rail\nDock\nTooltip\nAnimated Context Menu\nPopover\nMorphing Modal\nCenter Morph Modal\nText Animation\nNumber Animation\nAnimated Badge\nAction Swap\nAnimated Toast Stack\nTheme Toggle\nBouncy Accordion\nDrawer\nScroll Animation\nRange Slider\nWheel Picker\nTable\nShader Background\nCylinder Carousel\nLoader\nBLOCKS\n23\nInfinite Masonry\nNotification Stack\nProject Folder\nCard Folder\nFixtures\nAvailability Scheduler\nMulti-chain Swap\nDynamic Island\nCommand Palette\nMorphing Search\nExpandable Action Bar\nOverflow Actions\nExpandable Tabs\nMorphing Tabs\nSwipeable List\nFile Upload\nPrediction Market\nWallet Card\nOTP Input\nSign Up Form\nBloom Menu\nFeedback Widget\n404 / Not Found\nAI Agents\nMessage Scroller\nMessage Scroller\nCopy Page\n\nA reader-aware conversation viewport that follows streamed output at the live edge and releases control when the reader moves away.\n\nPreview\nPreview\nPreview\nUsage\nUsage\nCode\nCode\nWhat should the first release include?\nStart with the smallest workflow that still feels complete.\nInclude streaming and recovery states too.\nYes. Those states make the first version feel dependable.\nHow should we present tool results?\nKeep results close to the action that produced them.\nWhat about actions that need confirmation?\nPause the run, explain the impact, and ask before continuing.\nCan the transcript stay easy to navigate?\nUse the rail to jump between turns without losing your place.\nInstall\n\nAdd it with the shadcn CLI, or copy the source manually.\n\nCLI\nCLI\nManual\nManual\nbun\nbun\nnpm\nnpm\npnpm\npnpm\nyarn\nyarn\n$ bunx --bun shadcn add @beui/\nmessage-scroller\nmessage-scroller\nAPI Reference\nfollowOutput?\nboolean\n\nKeep streamed output pinned while the reader remains near the end.\n\ntrue\nfollowThreshold?\nnumber\n\nDistance from the end that still counts as following the output.\n\n56\nsmooth?\nboolean\n\nSmoothly follow growing content.\n\ntrue\nonFollowChange?\n((following: boolean) => void)\n\nReports when the reader leaves or returns to the live edge.\n\n—\nlabel?\nstring\n\nAccessible label for the scrollable transcript.\n\nConversation\nbusy?\nboolean\n\nMarks the transcript as waiting for more streamed content.\n\n—\nnavigation?\n\"rail\"\n\nAdds a compact rail for navigating between rendered Message rows.\n\n—\nnavigationLabel?\nstring\n\nAccessible label for the optional message navigation rail.\n\nMessage navigation\nviewportClassName?\nstring\n—\ncontentClassName?\nstring\n—\nrailClassName?\nstring\n—\nviewportRef?\nRef<HTMLElement>\n—\nviewportProps?\nOmit<DetailedHTMLProps<HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement>, HTMLElement>, \"children\" | \"ref\" | \"className\">\n—\ncontentProps?\nOmit<DetailedHTMLProps<HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, HTMLDivElement>, \"children\" | \"ref\" | \"className\">\n—\nclassName?\nstring\n—\nComposition\n\nKeep the scrolling viewport outside the message primitives it follows.\n\nMessageScroller\n└── MessageGroup\n    └── Message\n        └── MessageContent\n\nNote: Message provides stable, semantic rows for the transcript. Prompt Input starts new turns without owning transcript movement. Streaming Response supplies the growing content the viewport follows.\n\nHow it works\n\nA streaming transcript is not ordinary overflow. It must follow new output while the reader stays at the live edge, then stop moving the moment they choose to inspect earlier work.\n\nAlso on React Native. Follows new output and lets go when you scroll up.\nRelated components\nMessage\n\nComposable conversation primitives for message rows, grouped bubbles, avatars, metadata, live markers, and a mount-only trailing-edge pop-up for newly sent rows.\n\nChat App\n\nA complete agent conversation workspace composing navigation, messages, streaming, planning, approvals, tools, code, diffs, generated media, sources, and prompt input.\n\nTool Result\n\nA lightweight execution disclosure for syntax-highlighted terminal output and request responses that collapses into a compact completed state.\n\nAbout Message Scroller\n\nMessage Scroller is a React chat scroll container built for streaming AI responses. It follows new output while the reader sits at the bottom, stops following as soon as they scroll, swipe or press a key to read earlier messages, and resumes when they return to the live edge. An optional navigation rail lists the rendered messages as ticks with previews, highlights the one in view and scrolls to any message on click.\n\nWhen to use it\nAn AI chat app streams long answers and readers need to scroll back without being pulled down.\nA long agent transcript needs a compact rail to jump between earlier prompts and replies.\nA support chat shows a \"jump to latest\" button when the reader is no longer at the bottom.\nAccessibility\n\nThe viewport is a labeled section, and the content is a log role with a polite live region and aria-busy while you mark it busy, so screen readers hear new messages without interruption. Arrow Up, Page Up and Home, as well as wheel and touch, release following right away. Rail items have labels such as \"Go to user message 2 of 6\". With reduced motion enabled, following and rail navigation jump to position instead of scrolling smoothly.\n\nFAQ\nHow do I auto scroll a chat to the bottom in React without trapping the reader?\nWrap your messages in MessageScroller. followOutput keeps it pinned while the reader is within followThreshold pixels of the end, and onFollowChange reports when they leave or return, for example to show a jump to latest button.\nHow do I add message navigation?\nSet navigation to rail. The rail reads the rendered Message rows, builds previews from their text and appears once the transcript overflows. navigationLabel names it for screen readers.\nCan I use it with the Vercel AI SDK?\nYes. It only manages the viewport. Render your useChat messages as children and set busy while a response is streaming.\n\nUpdated Oct 23, 2026\n\nWeb\nWeb\nReact Native\nReact Native\nbeUI\nPro\nLimited Offer\n\n300+ blocks and premium motion components for React and Next.js.\n\n$179 lifetime access\n\nExplore beUI Pro\nSponsors\n\nDIAMOND\n\nTracwell\n\nVisitor insights for growth\n\nIllos\n\nAnimated illustrations for product sites\n\nBecome a sponsor",
